#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147295 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147616 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7da19110-4b7c-547a-bd79-b4df8088678b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Polyhedron Given Its Net"}] :question/id #uuid "8bca178c-5495-5205-b213-c75b8a4df3de" :question/math-academy-id "e-2759" :question/problem "The net of which polyhedron is shown below?\n\n![](images/96/96e7889a74d2d5bd35634ec022d3c9020d23fd7292b3bd7c05f8722860389645.png)" :question/worked-solution "We fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, as shown below.\n\n![](images/98/98ee3216b37bdce0081dd4daad1895cace7998a03d41c183184d07f6afaac126.png)\n\nAs a result, we get a triangular pyramid:\n\n![](images/32/32bdc8f811ca46a184307fa5521cb145cb0add8a0b4ee2bfae25add881561475.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147297 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147619 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe3ef90-285d-5dfa-b540-1a6c6826ecbe" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Net of a Polyhedron"}] :question/id #uuid "4501bf84-de3a-581f-b717-10996a285921" :question/math-academy-id "e-2761" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f233556f9055563f3956eea7eaf9744fb20993084f4c3eeb5e2e35d730d8d2aa.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the nets above is the net of a rectangular prism?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/5f/5fc1630e4e44bf68f833004ab975e406b8734fe062849484165310e093d14155.png)\n\n \n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a rectangular prism, as shown below: \n\n![](images/c2/c2f6985ca8cd95a71409936ede80c6f257e863bd459fe5a27178a04ea3edb88c.png)\n\n  \n\nNotice that the other two nets have triangular faces, so they cannot be the nets of a rectangular prism. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is I."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147300 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147620 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c8eb6c3d-6e29-59bb-af55-9dbb4be20b49" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Nets That Do Not Correspond to a Particular Polyhedron"}] :question/id #uuid "1e23f3ac-bcec-5070-b135-b2285d326bc4" :question/math-academy-id "e-2766" :question/problem "![](images/84/84f39f9d765a61db544fdddc7ee79859ab4a54c2e6f0e5018512723ca0dfcfd9.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the nets above is **not** the net of a pyramid?" :question/worked-solution "![](images/72/72462d252e84e20d567ccd10c2be12a6496f442f08d6e6baa609c5fb74f6fcc5.png)\n\n     \n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a triangular prism, as shown below: \n\n![](images/8e/8e77623f767c9cea456b787a09465397a4360915c547911a55927d8f7c9b4885.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the other two nets give us pyramids. Therefore,  the correct answer is I."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147303 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147621 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21ee2869-b51d-5bb3-82dc-7c8d48f229b7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Given Some Polyhedra Nets"}] :question/id #uuid "1b29a574-ac81-53cf-8dd7-3030e1f9bef3" :question/math-academy-id "e-2773" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e427a98c2953792d799190b7fc20a7dbf12ce014655316e21fb809e0abc9cdc5.png)\n\nWhich of the statements is true about the solids shown above?\n\nI. The net of solid I consists of triangles only.\n\nII. The net of solid II consists of $4$ triangles and $2$ rectangles.\n\nIII. The net of solid III consists of triangles only." :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the net of each solid.\n\n![](images/02/023f11b6924e6cf7318f54f5acdf910b1f688ee8ac40ec8f3b3ab7cd9c13c8df.png)\n\n \n\nNow, let's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false because the net of solid I consists of rectangles.\n\n- Statement II is false because the net of solid II consists of $2$ triangles and $3$ rectangles.\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566228 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147619 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8fe3ef90-285d-5dfa-b540-1a6c682